    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qnz7thd",
      "content": "Kerala is a state in the Indian Union governed by the Constitution of India. The state has a parliamentary system of government with a unicameral legislature. The Governor is the constitutional head, while the Chief Minister is the head of government."
