      "content": "3.5 Panchayati Raj in Kerala"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Kerala Panchayati Raj Act was passed in 1994 in accordance with the 73rd Constitutional Amendment.",
        "Kerala Legislative Assembly consists of 140 elected members.",
        "Questions on the first Chief Minister and Governor of Kerala are frequently asked in state competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "cj9yog4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7sihs4y",
      "content": "Kerala has a well-developed three-tier Panchayati Raj system. The state is a pioneer in decentralisation through the 'People's Plan Campaign' launched in 1996, which devolved significant funds, powers, and responsibilities to local governments."
    },
